Glooked[117Gnewer.[124GBut[128GA[130Gis[133Ga[135G[3mplan[140G[23mthat[145Ggot[149Grecorded[158Gafter[164Gthe[168Gwork[173Gwas[177Galready[185Gfinished.[195GThe[199Gcompiler[208Gread[213Gingestion[223Gorder[229Gas[232Gtruth[238Gorder[244G—[246Gthe[2C[1Bevent-time[14Gversus[21Gtruth-time[32Ggap[36Gyou[40Gasked[46Gabout[52Gweeks[58Gago,[63Gshowing[71Gup[74Gin[77Glive[82Gdata.[2C[1B[K[2C[1BTwo consequences:[K[2C[2B[1mThe c[9Goss-p[15Goject fil[25Ger prevented a wrong retireme[55Gt.[22m Not by design — it has no idea which claim is right.[111GIt refused because B belongs to another project, and that happened to be the correct outcom[203G. With s[212Gop[215G groups making sibling memory[245Gre[248Gdable,[2C[1Btha[8Gguard will also block legitimate cross-[51G supersedes. It logs [38;2;177;185;249mbad_supersede[39m when it[94Gfires,[101Gso[104Git's[109Gat[112Gleast[118Gvisible,[127Gbut[131G"no[135Glive[140Gmatch"[147Gdoesn't[155Gdistinguish[167G[3mwrong id[176G[23mfrom[181G[3mright id, wrong project[23m.[2C[2B[1mMy earlier recommendation still stands, and now I know it's the opposite of what the model wanted.[102G[22mClose[108GA,[111Gthe[115Gplan.[121GGround[128Gtruth[134Gis[137G[38;2;177;185;249mreranker.py:53 → MAX_DOC_CHARS = 4_000[39m,[177Gso[180GB[182Gis[185Gtrue.[191GHad[195Gthe[199Gsupersede[209Gsucceeded,[220Gyou'd[226Ghave[231Glost[236Gthe[240Gtrue[245Gclaim[251Gand[2C[1Bkept th[11G stale plan — and doctor would have report[56Gzero contradictions,[77Gcleanly[85Gwrong.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[32m# after the remember.py project fix[2C[1B[39mart[7Gr[9Gmember [36mrm[39m 348d379b-e329-4231-adf4-b4958c3ec6ed  [58G[32m# the plan[39m[K[2C[1Bart doctor --fix       [27G [29G       [37G     [43G    [48G    [53G   [57G  [32m# retire the dangling edge[86G[39m[K[2B [3GThe deeper issue —[22Gthat[27G"plan"[34Gand[38G"compl