9Gthe[143Gextraction[154Gfine;[160Gthe[164G[3mjudgment[173G[23mis[176Gwhere[182Git[185Gmight[191Gslip,[197Gand[201Gthat's[208Gwhat[213Gfeeds[219Gyour[224Ggraph.[1B[K[1B  It's directly measurable, though: run the same real batch through both and compare the facts, the dedupe decisions, and the relations. Worth remembering the bar isn't sky-high — the false contradiction we fixed an hour ago, where a plan was ruled to[K[1B  supersede its own completed outcome, came from the 27B.[K[2B [3GWant me to set bot[22G servers up and run that comparison on a live batch? It's[80Gconfig-only on the[99Garteries[108Gside,[114Gand[118GI'd[122Ggive[127Gyou[131Ga[133Gside-by-side[146Gbefore[153Gyou[157Gcommit[164Gto[167Git.[2B[38;2;153;153;153m✻[3GS[5Gutéed for[15G2m 22s ·[24G1 shell still running[2B[48;2;55;55;55m[38;2;80;80;80m❯ [38;2;255;255;255mDo these first: 1. Drop the RERANKER_DEVICE line from the hooks. Free, and it restores the behaviour capillaries intended — pick the emptiest card, don't fall back to CPU [39m                                                                                 [1B  [38;2;255;255;255m2. Load in bfloat16. 2.4 GB → 1.2 GB, no quality cost.[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                      [1B  [38;2;255;255;255m3. Raise MIN_FREE_VRAM to ~6 GB and drop batch_size to 8. Honest about activations; the batch is the biggest single lever.[39m                                                                                                                                  [2C[2B[49mStar[8Ging with the hooks[27G— including th[42G ge[46Gerator,[54Gor[57G[38;2;177;185;249mart setup --sync[74G[39mwould[80Gput[84Gthe[88Gline[93Gback.[6C[2B[38;2;153;153;153m[1m2[22G[22ms [2C[2B[39mNow[7Gthe capillaries[23Gside[28G— bfloat16,[40Gt[43G VRAM[49Gthr[53Gshold, a[62Gd[64Gthe batch.[75G[K[6C[2B[38;2;153;153;153m[1m2[22G[22ms [2C[2B[39mNow [9Gsting it actually loads and [38Gc[41Ges in bf16.[K[6C[2B[38;2;153;153;153m[1m1[22G[22m [39m[K[2C[2BThe[7Gdtype[13Gcame back bf16 on CPU even wh[43Gre my code pass[59Gs no[64Gdtype — so sentence-transformers[97Galr[101Gady honors the[116Gche[120Gkpoint dtype.[134GLet[138Gme[141Gverify[148Gthat[153Gproperly,[163Gbecause[171Git[174Gmeans[180Gmy[183Gbf16[188Gclaim[194Gwas[198Gwrong.[2B [3G[38;2;153;153;153mRan [1m1[22m shell command [39m[K[1B[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39mMy[6Gitem 2 was wrong. sentence-transformers 5.7.0 already loads[66Gthe[70Gcheckpoint[81Gdtype[87G—[89Gbf16,[95G1.11[100GGB.[104GThere[110Gwas[114Gno[117Gfp32[122Gupcast[129Gto[132Gfix,[137Gso[140Gthat[145Gchange[152Gis[155Ga[157Gno-op.[164GReverting[174Git.[5C[1B[K[2C[1B[38;2;153;153;153mRan [1m2[22m shell commands [1B[39m[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[39m GPU 1 has 6.6 GB free — just over the new bar, so autodetect will pick it. That's exactly the case that OOM'd[113Gat[116Gbatch[122G16.[126GTesting[134Git.[2B[38;2;153;153;153m●[39m Keeping waiting for the run[38;2;153;153;153m · 1m 3s[39m[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  $ SP=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-bao-tn-Coding-Projects-arteries/a2be0826-975e-439d-94e8-27128a088dd7/scratchpad; for i in $(seq 1 29); do grep -q "EXIT=" $SP/search-fixed.log 2>/dev/null && break; sleep 4; done; tail -3 $SP/search-fixed.log; echo " [5C[1Bdots: $(tr -cd '.' < $SP/search-fixed.log | wc -c)" (1m 0s)[2C[1B[39m   [38;2;153;153;153m(ctrl+b to run in background)[2C[1B[39m[K[1B[38;2;215;119;87m·[3G[38;2;225;139;107mBooping…[38;2;215;119;87m [38;2;153;153;153m(6m 0s · ↓[39m [38;2;153;153;153m7.5k tokens)[39m[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  Tip: Ask Claude to create a todo list when working on complex tasks to track progress and 